Rack Registry

Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs

Rack Registry is an open-source, vendor-neutral runtime that establishes the
canonical physical model of racks inside a data center: which racks exist, how
they are composed, what occupies them, which generation of that composition is
authoritative, and which claims about it must be rejected as stale.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Rack Registry does not collect or transmit any telemetry. It opens no network
sockets, performs no name resolution, and contacts no remote service. All state
it writes is written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the
machine running the software.

Rack Registry accepts contributions from individuals and organizations on the
